{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Change 26 (post-epic addition, operator-proposed): epic-close bug gate -> ticket 4b54-6e28-45f7-42db under epic 2f4c. Evaluated the proposal logically and against the event-level record (STATUS events from the tickets branch, not updated_at proxies — two adjudications corrected: 22f5 was fixed in-epic before close; 5e94 was created 13 days post-close). Real at-close escapes: 30a2, 5b09 (2/56 closes). Design: DET caused_by floor + DET candidate filter (created-after-first-in_progress OR linked-any-depth; commit-relation criterion rejected on evidence: 0 unique catches, 2 FPs, 58% cited-SHA rot) + single-turn haiku forced-choice screen (cached epic prefix, warm-then-parallel, model-class config) forwarding max 8 compact candidates to the completion verifier, which adjudicates via its native show_ticket tool and blocks only undispositioned deliverable-defects. Screen tally recorded in sidecar; degrades open; regression set encoded in the ticket. Backtest scripts: /tmp/bt_epic_bugs.py, /tmp/bt_filter.py, /tmp/bt_c3b.py."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785690284140399001,"uuid":"63a45b47-5be0-4b3e-9d07-96cb7158b8fe"}